// Two DIFFERENT keys deliberately sharing a hashCode -> collision
class BadKey {
    final String name;
    BadKey(String n) { name = n; }
    public int hashCode() { return 42; }          // everyone collides!
    public boolean equals(Object o) {
        return o instanceof BadKey b && b.name.equals(name);
    }
}
Map<BadKey, Integer> m = new HashMap<>();
m.put(new BadKey("a"), 1);   // bucket 42
m.put(new BadKey("b"), 2);   // SAME bucket -> chained, both kept
System.out.println(m.get(new BadKey("a")));  // 1 - equals finds it in the chain
// All keys in one bucket => lookups degrade toward O(n)/O(log n).
```

