Map<String, Integer> map = new HashMap<>();
map.put("apple", 1);     // hashCode("apple") -> bucket index
map.put("apple", 2);     // same key: equals() true -> overwrites to 2
System.out.println(map.get("apple"));   // 2

// Custom key MUST override hashCode AND equals or lookups fail:
record Point(int x, int y) {}        // record auto-generates both
Map<Point, String> grid = new HashMap<>();
grid.put(new Point(1, 2), "A");
System.out.println(grid.get(new Point(1, 2)));  // "A" - found
```
A new object with the same fields finds the entry only because `hashCode`/`equals` agree.

```java
// BROKEN: equals overridden, hashCode NOT -> lookup fails
class BadId {
    final int id; BadId(int id){ this.id = id; }
    public boolean equals(Object o){ return o instanceof BadId b && b.id==id; }
    // inherits Object.hashCode() -> different per instance!
}
Map<BadId,String> m1 = new HashMap<>();
m1.put(new BadId(7), "X");
System.out.println(m1.get(new BadId(7)));   // null! wrong bucket

// CORRECT: record generates equals AND hashCode together
record GoodId(int id) {}
Map<GoodId,String> m2 = new HashMap<>();
m2.put(new GoodId(7), "X");
System.out.println(m2.get(new GoodId(7)));  // "X"
```

